 "sentences": [
  {
   "text": "In 1869, a scientist made a sunset in a glass tube, and almost explained why the sky is blue.",
   "s": 0.0,
   "e": 4.895
  },
  {
   "text": "London, 1869. John Tyndall is scrubbing the dust out of the air in his basement laboratory.",
   "s": 5.075,
   "e": 10.505
  },
  {
   "text": "He fills a glass tube with smoke and fires a beam of light through it.",
   "s": 10.605,
   "e": 13.363
  },
  {
   "text": "From the side, the beam glows blue. From the end, it comes out orange.",
   "s": 13.443,
   "e": 17.501
  },
  {
   "text": "Outside his window, the real sky is blue, and the air is clear.",
   "s": 17.601,
   "e": 21.172
  },
  {
   "text": "One problem: the real sky has no smoke in it.",
   "s": 21.292,
   "e": 23.698
  },
  {
   "text": "Luckily, the colours were right. Unluckily, the reason was wrong.",
   "s": 23.898,
   "e": 27.726
  },
  {
   "text": "You see, smoke particles are big and lumpy. Air molecules are a thousand times smaller, and tiny obstacles scatter short waves far more than long ones.",
   "s": 27.946,
   "e": 35.591
  },
  {
   "text": "Blue is scattered about six times more than red.",
   "s": 35.691,
   "e": 37.8
  },
  {
   "text": "Think of a speed bump: a bicycle feels every bump; a truck rolls straight over them. Blue is the bicycle; red is the truck.",
   "s": 37.92,
   "e": 44.241
  },
  {
   "text": "At noon, blue light bounces across the whole sky and into your eye from every direction.",
   "s": 44.361,
   "e": 48.173
  },
  {
   "text": "At sunset, sunlight cuts through thirty-eight times more air, the blue is scattered away, and red comes through.",
   "s": 48.273,
   "e": 53.37
  },
  {
   "text": "Two years later, a young Englishman named John Strutt \u2014 the future Lord Rayleigh \u2014 did the maths and showed the air itself could do it.",
   "s": 53.49,
   "e": 59.399
  },
  {
   "text": "The rule is called Rayleigh scattering. It explains why the Moon's sky is black and why Mars's sky is butterscotch.",
   "s": 59.499,
   "e": 65.196
  },
  {
   "text": "So the sky is blue because the air is stealing the blue from the sun.",
   "s": 65.316,
   "e": 68.176
  },
  {
   "text": "The sunset is the receipt.",
   "s": 68.376,
   "e": 69.591
  }
 ]
}